  "content": {
    "id": "p29-cc-4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Bob is tasked to simplify $\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}-\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}$, but is confused because the formula he has learned has no fractions. Explain how Bob can still use the formula to simplify the given expression.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\cos\\theta$.\n\nUse $\\frac{\\theta}{2}$ as the input angle in the cosine double-angle identity.",
      "worked": "The identity $\\cos 2u=\\cos^2u-\\sin^2u$ applies to any angle $u$. Set $u=\\frac{\\theta}{2}$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}-\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\cos\\left(2\\times\\frac{\\theta}{2}\\right)\\\\\\cos^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}-\\sin^2\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\cos\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
